{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/713109-metis-and-rank","id":713109,"title":"Metis and rank?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-21T15:47:04-07:00","id":713109,"title":"Metis and rank?","content":"I think it's pretty clear by now that metis is my favourite breed out of the three in WtA. Due to playing so many, though, I've gotten into pondering one aspect of them that seems to confuse even the writers sometimes.<br /> <br /> What is rank to a metis?<br /> <br /> Or, rather, how a metis of a rank should be treated. I've seen few omega metis in books/games at rank 3, and it often confused me, because then it went against the rank system. And while I can definitely see metis being given less than someone of their rank, rank is still rank. How much messing with the litany has to be done so it would be justified?<br /> <br /> So, I've basically taken to believing metis of rank are the ones that managed to somewhat break through the disdain others have for them to challenge for the rank and succeed. They are considered their rank, if not the lesser of that rank. Any metis who is less lucky is stuck as cliath, because they were never given the chance to challenge due their metis status. This way, the omega metis -are- always lesser, and so it won't create any strange rank vs breed issues.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T16:49:26-07:00","id":713190,"title":"","content":"The higher a Metis's Rank, the less stigma he should face<br /> <br /> I've got the impression that in premodern times, Metis had to EARN the right to go through a Rite of passage<br /> <br /> these days they usualy gain it soon after Adolescence, like all garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T00:38:58-07:00","id":713886,"title":"","content":"I think that it used to be that for tribes BESIDES Bone Gnawers and Children of Gaia, being a Metis was a dead end in life. Now, Garou can't afford for the Metis to NOT be able to pull there own weight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T00:59:37-07:00","id":713918,"title":"","content":"It is not easy for Metis to attain rank, but those that do are damn worthy of respect. Werewolves are very hierarchical; treat a higher-ranking Metis badly and you are asking to get your teeth kicked in by a mule.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T02:34:01-07:00","id":714053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/713109-metis-and-rank?p=713918#post713918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not easy for Metis to attain rank, but those that do are damn worthy of respect. Werewolves are very hierarchical; treat a higher-ranking Metis badly and you are asking to get your teeth kicked in by a mule.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This. They might need a bit more renown to get their Rank, but Rank in Werewolf is earned, not gifted. And anyone who has the chops to have a Rank is not someone you want to fuck with. Sure, they might tell nasty stories about them behind their backs, but when they have something to say they will listen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T02:48:22-07:00","id":714061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/713109-metis-and-rank?p=714053#post714053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. They might need a bit more renown to get their Rank, but Rank in Werewolf is earned, not gifted. And anyone who has the chops to have a Rank is not someone you want to fuck with. Sure, they might tell nasty stories about them behind their backs, but when they have something to say they will listen.</div> </div> </div> </div>And exactly -this- is why it always annoys me up when I see a metis NPC who is rank 2+ and still the lowest of the sept. Outside mere stats, why the heck have that character have rank that means nothing? The infamous rank 4 Children of Gaia metis galliard not being able to sing at moots is the culmination of this.<br /> <br /> For tribes like the Fianna, I can't help but think most are stuck as cliath until they leave their home septs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T03:26:05-07:00","id":714082,"title":"","content":"Wasn't that rank 4 Metis Galilard in the Children of Gaia tribebook? That should tell you all you need to know about that fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T03:31:20-07:00","id":714097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/713109-metis-and-rank?p=714082#post714082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't that rank 4 Metis Galilard in the Children of Gaia tribebook? That should tell you all you need to know about that fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, no. It was in Guardians of the Caern's metis section. As in, the one where there would be most info on the breed. Hence why it is so baffling XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T03:48:15-07:00","id":714111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/713109-metis-and-rank?p=714097#post714097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sadly, no. It was in Guardians of the Caern's metis section. As in, the one where there would be most info on the breed. Hence why it is so baffling XD</div> </div> </div> </div>That one wasn't a stellar piece, either. Player's guide to the Garou and Book of Auspices were so much better on explaining Garou society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T04:10:51-07:00","id":714130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/713109-metis-and-rank?p=714111#post714111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That one wasn't a stellar piece, either. Player's guide to the Garou and Book of Auspices were so much better on explaining Garou society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, definitely! But if a book has a metis section, most are still gonna take stuff from it.<br /> <br /> Changing Ways can't come soon enough..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T16:30:31-07:00","id":720954,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Good topic. I think in my games from now on when ever a metis character or npc does or say something of note for or before others I will get them to roll the appropriate renown trait permenant dots. Wheres homid and lupus will just get a ...he's a higher rank, best listen and do.<br /> If the roll fails...'sucks to be you mule'<br /> if the roll succeeds.... 'hmm this explains why the metis has lived so long. '","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T16:47:20-07:00","id":721022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/713109-metis-and-rank?p=720954#post720954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Good topic. I think in my games from now on when ever a metis character or npc does or say something of note for or before others I will get them to roll the appropriate renown trait permenant dots. Wheres homid and lupus will just get a ...he's a higher rank, best listen and do.<br /> If the roll fails...'sucks to be you mule'<br /> if the roll succeeds.... 'hmm this explains why the metis has lived so long. '</div> </div> </div> </div>So they'd disrespect someone of higher rank outright? Why have a character of rank, if the rank doesn't truly matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T17:38:01-07:00","id":721229,"title":"","content":"Because you can challenge someone above or below you by a margin if you disagree, dislike, or want the opportunity they have to be yours before the eyes your peers in garou society.<br /> Especially to a metis who might be above you and if that offends you. Which it should. Dont get me wrong i love those loveable, deep, traumatic, emotional, cursed beings that are wonderful...but ultimately scum in garou culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T18:05:52-07:00","id":721298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/713109-metis-and-rank?p=721229#post721229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because you can challenge someone above or below you by a margin if you disagree, dislike, or want the opportunity they have to be yours before the eyes your peers in garou society.<br /> Especially to a metis who might be above you and if that offends you. Which it should. Dont get me wrong i love those loveable, deep, traumatic, emotional, cursed beings that are wonderful...but ultimately scum in garou culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is simply challenges, though. Rank still comes with priviledges that one in lower rank can't match. And we're not talking about Cliath vs Fostern, but Cliath vs Adren or Athro here. That, and not all tribes will so actively put a metis down.<br /> <br /> Also, rank is earned, not given. A metis with rank above cliath has earned enough renown and respect from others to be worthy of challenging and succeeded in the challenge. So even if they are not liked, they have clearly earned their place to hold that rank. To lack the benefits even after ranking up is to say garou can ignore another's rank and renown if they don't feel like respecting them. Which happens, but still goes against the Litany.<br /> <br /> None of this means metis will have an easy time with their peers of rank, but they now are scum that has to be tolerated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T18:38:20-07:00","id":721386,"title":"","content":"Well in that scenario it wouldn't be the cliath and fostern disrespecting or holding the Adren or Athro Metis down. It'd be the other Athros, the Elders.<br /> <br /> in the case of the Athro Galliard that cant sing at a moot it could be any number of reasons. Off the top of my head, the Sept Alpha hates or distrusts all metis and has decreed it so their and the other elders sensibilities arent offended during an important and auspious event.<br /> <br /> Perhaps they feel the Metis feelings and voice although deep and meaningful could challenge the order of their leadership and traditions if went un checked.<br /> <br /> perhaps along with a lot of traditions, benefits and priviledges that are held at the sept for those of rank that there is also an anothet rule made long ago that metis can be seen but not heard and the leaders and others of rank are cautious what changing one rule might encourage others to challenge or demand change too.<br /> <br /> lots of reaons (in garou culture) to keep a metis down. Not a lot of reasons to lift them up. Or undo thousands of years of tradition, fear, disgust and prejudice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T17:44:25-07:00","id":724591,"title":"","content":"Isn't the point of the Renown system that once you've proved yourself of something everyone has to accept that you have earned your stripes? I can see political manouvering and ways of undermining Metis who are in high rank positions, but actually fucking with them in public is suicidal politically and physically. The litany says that you have to respect those of higher station (at least in public, anything they cannot pin on you is fair game), doing this shit means you literally break the Litany. That's a direct penalty to your renown and grounds for actual punishments from the Philodoxes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:18:36-07:00","id":726712,"title":"","content":"Rank should function as normal. However, other Garou will abuse the system &quot;subtly&quot; in ways that they can justify they are obeying customs as normal. They will try to avoid outright blatant violation of Garou custom. In terms of discrimination against Metis, this is what I see:<br /> <br /> Metis have a harder time getting recognition for temporary renown.<br /> Metis have to wait longer to have the Rite of Accomplishment performed, and likely other Garou are more likely to dispute the rite.<br /> <br /> The combined effect is that Metis increase rank at a noticeably slower pace than non-Metis.<br /> <br /> For Garou of the same rank, they likely treat any Metis with the least amount of respect and honor.<br /> Garou of one rank lower are more likely to challenge them or treat them as equal.<br /> <br /> The combined effect is that it seems the Metis is functionally one rank lower than he is in reality.<br /> <br /> However, the Metis is of that rank. And if privileges or honors are accorded to that rank, septs have to give it to the Metis. While it is possible for a sept to outright violate Garou customs to blatantly persecute a Metis outside of certain boundaries, this should be relatively rare because it will bring dishonor on them. The dishonor does not come from treating a Metis badly or unfairly, but for violating ancient Garou customs and offending ancestors and the litany. Tradition should be sacred enough that blatant violation of it for any reason forces the Nation to intervene at some point. If a Rank 4 Galliard is able to sing at moots, then even a Metis rank 4 galliard must be able to do so.<br /> <br /> I would say in the case where a sept prevents a Rank 4 Galliard from singing at a moot continually, that it creates a big scandal. That may have the effect of reducing Honor renown attained at that sept, or have appropriate tribal Elders from other septs show up to put the house in order. If the Garou at the sept refuse to change their ways, I can see moon bridges being closed, not taking visitors from said sept, having promising sept members defect to other septs, and so on. Again, this won't be done to support the Metis. It will be done to preserve the Traditions of the Garou. In fact, while indirectly helping the Metis in question, those Garou Elders likely blame him for creating the problem to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T06:51:05-07:00","id":734589,"title":"","content":"It would be the metis' fault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}